    "narrative": "Our optimal path today centers on **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (79.25) and **Cal Raleigh** (74.89), our two clear-cut starts. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a soft 4.82 xERA matchup against Barnett, and despite facing a catcher with a 57% hold rate, his volume in the #2 hole makes him our primary engine for counting stats. **Cal Raleigh** enters a favorable park environment against Hughes; while the platoon split against a righty presents a marginal headwind, the projected run-scoring environment elevates his profile significantly. **Dylan Beavers** (67.10) also emerges as a high-upside play, leveraging a massive +16% park boost and the protection of the leadoff spot to overcome the threat of May\u2019s 63% hold rate.\n\nThe decision to bench **Jonathan Aranda** (44.51) was the most difficult call of the morning. While he holds a strong base projection, a -12% platoon penalty against Suarez (L) pushed him just below the threshold required to displace **Kyle Karros** or the outfield trio. We are exercising caution with **Lawrence Butler** (52.29) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (44.57) today; both face Espino and Glasnow respectively\u2014two of the toughest arms on the slate\u2014resulting in significant downward pressure on their scores due to SP skill deficits. We are keeping **Zack Gelof** and **Masyn Winn** firmly on the bench as their sub-40 scores indicate they are strictly below our efficiency floor for protecting game caps. \n\nMonitor the late-inning situation for **Jeremiah Jackson** (54.17) and **Dylan Beavers**; May\u2019s high hold percentage makes them primary targets for pinch-hitting maneuvers if they fail to reach base early. Conversely, we expect **Will Smith** (60.29) to provide a stable floor in the #2 spot against Perdomo, though his value is tethered to the 4.23 xERA holding steady. No major weather concerns have been flagged, but with several starters facing sub-4.00 xERA arms, efficiency remains the priority to ensure we maximize our category output in the home stretch.",
